# AMD64 thunk export spec -- psapi.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 corpus pass.  Styx: Master of Shadows imports this
# module STATICALLY -- and so does the EasyHook64.dll it ships -- and it had
# no guest thunk, so the loader refused the native ppc64 module (c000007b) and
# the whole image failed to load (c0000135).  Measured: the exe's import table
# names GetPerformanceInfo and GetProcessMemoryInfo, and nothing else.
DLL psapi.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# psapi.h is the one case where the module's own public header RENAMES the
# entire API.  With PSAPI_VERSION > 1, which is the default the header itself
# sets, psapi.h #defines all 27 names to their K32* equivalents BEFORE
# declaring them, so what the translation unit ends up declaring is
# K32GetProcessMemoryInfo and the oracle looking up the export name
# psapi.spec publishes -- GetProcessMemoryInfo -- finds nothing.  PROBE-EXTRA
# alone does not fix this: the header still declares only the K32* name.
#
# PROBE-DEFINE PSAPI_VERSION=1 makes psapi.h skip the rename and declare the
# plain names directly (psapi.h:24-26 only defaults PSAPI_VERSION when it is
# not already defined).  The signature is identical either way --
# K32GetModuleFileNameExW and GetModuleFileNameExW share one prototype -- so
# this asks the oracle the question psapi.spec's own export names pose,
# rather than guessing an answer for it.  PROBE-EXTRA is still needed because
# psapi.h is not in the oracle's default translation unit (see PROBE_SRC in
# wine_sig.py): no PROBE-EXTRA means psapi.h is never read at all, define or
# no define.
#
# The same macro-rename hides ten of wldap32's exports, but by a DIFFERENT
# mechanism -- winldap.h's WINELIB_NAME_AW(), keyed on UNICODE, not a
# module-local version switch -- so it does not take this same PROBE-DEFINE
# treatment; see wldap32.thunks and ppc64le/games/STATUS.md.
PROBE-EXTRA psapi.h
PROBE-DEFINE PSAPI_VERSION=1
